Subject: [PATCH 113/116] drm/msm/a6xx: Let the GMU vote the A620 DDR bandwidth

Describe the SH0/MC0/ACV BCMs as on A621, so that the GMU gets a
bandwidth table built from the opp-peak-kBps of each GPU level and votes
DDR itself with every frequency change. Tested with the a650 GMU
firmware 2.1.8: no regression in GPU memory bandwidth (6.1-6.9 GB/s for
a texture copy at 540 MHz, same as with Linux interconnect votes).

These changes were written with the help of an LLM and checked by a human.

Assisted-by: LLM dtschema
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RmfiVDW3KWZdb9c3iDGRYg
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
index ff38f394c..a9d54c6f7 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
@@ -909,6 +909,16 @@ static const struct adreno_info a6xx_gpus[] = {
 			.gbif_cx = a640_gbif,
 			.gmu_cgc_mode = 0x00020202,
 			.prim_fifo_threshold = 0x00010000,
+			.bcms = (const struct a6xx_bcm[]) {
+				{ .name = "SH0", .buswidth = 16 },
+				{ .name = "MC0", .buswidth = 4 },
+				{
+					.name = "ACV",
+					.fixed = true,
+					.perfmode = BIT(3),
+				},
+				{ /* sentinel */ },
+			},
 		},
 		.speedbins = ADRENO_SPEEDBINS(
 			{ 0,    0 },
